From 851c78fd8209ac5c8bc727be5dd4bfc1c9b964e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: akapug <akapug@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 13:43:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/22] sycl: flash attention via oneMKL: a row per work-group
 softmax, and no host waits

The prefill path (32+ query tokens, KV 1024+) spent most of its time outside the GEMMs:
- the online softmax ran one work-item per query row, walking the row twice with strided
  reads (3072 work-items for a GQA-6 ubatch of 512); now a work-group per row holds the
  row in registers, reads it once, coalesced (4 at a time when strides allow), and reduces
  across the group;
- the host waited after every step (per KV head: after the Q pack, and per chunk after the
  K/V copy, each GEMM and the softmax); everything is on the one in-order queue, which
  oneMKL enqueues its GEMMs on, so the device now runs the steps back to back (the
  GGML_SYCL_MKL_FA_DEBUG timers still wait, to time each step);
- f16 K/V was copied into a dense chunk before each GEMM; it is now the GEMM operand in
  place, with its row stride (quantized K/V is still dequantized per chunk);
- the S x V GEMM wrote a chunk result that a separate kernel added into the accumulator; it
  now accumulates directly (beta = 1 after the softmax rescaled the accumulator);
- the output normalize ran a work-item per row; it is now a work-item per element.
Arc Pro B70, FLASH_ATTN_EXT head dim 256, 4 K/V heads, GQA 6, f16 K/V, 512 query tokens:
KV 4096 6.09 -> 1.69 ms, 16384 22.4 -> 6.78 ms, 32768 44.0 -> 13.4 ms (9.4 -> 30.8 TFLOPS).
Ternary Bonsai 2 27B pp512: at depth 16384 ~400 -> 703 tok/s, at 32768 386 -> 616 tok/s.
FLASH_ATTN_EXT 4091/4091.
